# ============================================================================
# 2K Football Mod Tools — public beta repository ignore list
#
# This workspace doubles as a private reverse-engineering lab.  NOTHING retail
# or bulky may ever be committed: no game images, no extracted game data, no
# Ghidra projects, no build artifacts.  The release archives shipped as GitHub
# Release assets are independently verified retail-free by the packaging gate.
# ============================================================================

# --- Retail game data (NEVER commit) ---------------------------------------
ESPN NFL 2K5 (USA).xiso.iso
extracted/
All-Pro Football 2K8 (USA)/
*.iso
*.qcow2

# --- Build outputs / artifacts / asset caches ------------------------------
build/
build-clang/
build-sanitize/
build-static-recomp-apf/
artifacts/
assets/

# --- Ghidra / reverse-engineering heavy data -------------------------------
ghidra_projects/
research/
tools/vendor/
tools/ghidra-home/
tools/__pycache__/
tools/generated/

# --- Generated reports (large).  Small pinned specs are kept. --------------
reports/assets/
reports/cut_content/
reports/static_recomp/
reports/manifests/
reports/headers/
reports/asset_samples/
reports/cross_title/

# --- Internal-only documentation (large PDF/HTML dossiers) -----------------
docs/updates/

# --- Local working / scratch / agent state ---------------------------------
.codex-tmp/
.codex/
.agents/
.geometry-proof/
.pytest_cache/
release-staging/

# --- Python ---------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# --- CI / test tooling caches ----------------------------------------------
# The CI workflow (.github/workflows/ci.yml) runs the suite as standalone
# scripts (bytecode goes to __pycache__/, ignored above) and stages the
# release gates under the runner's temp dir, never inside the workspace, so a
# CI run leaves the tree clean.  These cover the incidental caches a coverage,
# type-check, or local test run can still drop.
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.hypothesis/
.tox/
.nox/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

# --- OS / editor cruft ----------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*~

# --- Stray media ----------------------------------------------------------
*.mp4
*.avi
*.mkv
*.png.tmp

# --- MyCareer hub backdrop: composed from the user's own disc at build time ---
# docs/mycareer_art/build.py decodes the Crib skyline texture through the private
# source cache; the composed backdrop, the mockups drawn on it and its P8 previews
# are retail-derived and stay local. The recipe, atlases and check report are kept.
docs/mycareer_art/mycareer_apartment.png
docs/mycareer_art/hub_mockup_*.png
docs/mycareer_art/*_hub_mockup_*.png
docs/mycareer_art/previews/preview_*_mycareer_apartment.png
